From 5671bb6915d200e499575c81915f905d01ec2d0e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ferran Duarri <ferran.duarri@me.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 15:55:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] apparmor: advertise unconfined userns-restriction support via
 securityfs

Ubuntu's own apparmor.service checks
/sys/kernel/security/apparmor/features/policy/unconfined_restrictions/userns
at every boot (rc.apparmor.functions::check_and_set_userns()) before
trusting kernel.apparmor_restrict_unprivileged_userns. If that securityfs
boolean is absent, it concludes the running kernel doesn't support
unconfined-userns restriction and force-sets the sysctl back to 0, logging
"disabling unprivileged userns restrictions since unconfined userns is
not supported / enabled".

0024 (John Johansen's Ubuntu SAUCE, forward-ported) wired the real
enforcement (apparmor_userns_create(), aa_profile_ns_perm(),
AA_USERNS_CREATE) but never added this advertisement entry, so Ubuntu's
own boot script silently undoes the restriction on every boot even though
the kernel-side mediation works and does not itself depend on this file.
Found and root-caused on the 7.2.0-hyphaed boot audit, 2026-08-27: sysctl
read 0 despite 10-apparmor.conf setting 1.

Add "userns" next to the existing "change_profile" boolean in
aa_sfs_entry_unconfined[], matching the shape apparmor.service already
expects. Advertisement only -- no enforcement path changes, so this
carries no behavior change beyond letting the boot script stop overriding
the sysctl. Compiled clean: security/apparmor/apparmorfs.o.

Not John Johansen's work -- ours, addressing a gap his port left.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Ferran Duarri <ferran.duarri@me.com>
---
 security/apparmor/apparmorfs.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/security/apparmor/apparmorfs.c b/security/apparmor/apparmorfs.c
index 56155d7d5..5fb39fd1d 100644
--- a/security/apparmor/apparmorfs.c
+++ b/security/apparmor/apparmorfs.c
@@ -2460,6 +2460,7 @@ static struct aa_sfs_entry aa_sfs_entry_domain[] = {
 
 static struct aa_sfs_entry aa_sfs_entry_unconfined[] = {
 	AA_SFS_FILE_BOOLEAN("change_profile", 1),
+	AA_SFS_FILE_BOOLEAN("userns", 1),
 	{ }
 };
 
